  "cut_point": "We are asked to find how many **four-digit numbers** formed by the digits **1, 2, 3** can have a **sum of 10**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Total digits used in a four-digit number\n\nEach digit in a four-digit number is used **exactly once**, and we are allowed to repeat the digits **up to 3 times**.",
  "reflection": {
    "verified_state": [
      "We need to count four-digit numbers formed by the digits 1, 2, and 3 whose digit sum is 10."
    ],
    "error_step": "Each digit in a four-digit number is used **exactly once**, and we are allowed to repeat the digits **up to 3 times**.",
    "error_reason": "This is contradictory and imposes a false restriction: repeated use means a digit such as 1 can appear any number of times, including all four positions, so there is no \"up to 3 times\" limit.",
    "new_direction": "Treat the four-digit number as an ordered quadruple of digits from {1,2,3} and count all quadruples whose sum is 10."
  }
